/* @kp-soft/themes v11.0.0 — css/themes.css
   The seven house themes as plain CSS custom properties, plus the shared
   register/texture machinery. No Tailwind here: a Tailwind v4 consumer
   also imports css/tailwind-bridge.css; the cyberpunk register (HUD
   chrome, motion) lives in css/cyberpunk-register.css and is opt-in.
   Extracted from kp-soft resources/css/app.css at commit 2983abb on
   2026-09-02. Status tokens (--status-*) are new in this package.

   GENERATED — do not edit this file. The token blocks below come from
   themes/<name>/tokens.json; everything after them from css/_rules.css.
   Change those and run `npm run generate`. A gate refuses a commit where
   this file does not match its source (T3, AR2, AR3). The first line of
   this comment is a contract value: two consumers anchor on it. */

/* The cascade order [AR17]. Layer order beats specificity, which is the
   whole reason this exists: a single-class utility could never win against
   a component rule like `.kp-table td` on specificity alone, whatever the
   file order. Consequence taken deliberately: a consumer's own UNLAYERED
   CSS wins over everything here, components included — which is the right
   default for a package whose posture is that a consumer overrides it.
   Token declarations stay outside the layers.
   kp.signature [scope-140] holds each theme's approved signature for the
   progress bar and ten elements, at the end of its register file: it comes
   right after kp.register, so it draws over the register as the approved
   demos did, whatever the weight of a register selector. */
@layer kp.base, kp.components, kp.register, kp.signature, kp.layout, kp.utilities;

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   The seven themes (T1, T9). Each block is a COMPLETE token set; the
   contrast checker (scripts/check-contrast.mjs) fails the build when
   any pair drops under WCAG AA (T3). Fallback (no data-theme) = formal.
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

