 * --kp-entity-actions-gap (the air between the last meter and the actions, --kp-space-md). The buttons come only from the data:
 * no action, no row.
 * The trend row [gap-entity-tiles-1019] is one more row of the meters block (label, a 24-hour line, the current value, on the
 * meters' own columns); `--kp-entity-meters` counts it, so the card's rows need no new template. The line is the KPI tile's
 * sparkline (js/kpi.js drawSparkline) with its own parts, `.kp-entity__spark-line` and `-area`; knob --kp-entity-spark (the line's colour, --chart-1).
 * The tile [gap-entity-tiles-1019] (`.kp-card--entity[data-kp-entity-tile]`, js/entity-card.js `data-kp-entity-kind="tile"`) is the
 * same card with four rows (identity, state, description, lines) and no actions: the name's link covers the whole card, the star
 * and the Retry stand above it, the description takes what room is left and the lines sit at the foot of every tile alike.
 * Knobs: --kp-entity-tile-body (the least height of the description, 2.75rem), --kp-entity-min (16rem on a tile grid). */
    .kp-entity-grid {
